From e966744a6db8d2d699931d88e1aa313103274922 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chao Chen <209239467+surlymochan@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 00:47:12 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(dev): run the pre-commit hook and dev checks from a
 subdirectory or worktree

The pre-commit hook, staged-typecheck, dev-verify, prepare-dev-environment
and check-release-notes assumed that OpenBot is the root of its git
repository. When OpenBot is checked out as a subdirectory of a larger
repository, git reports paths from the repository root, so the checks
missed every staged file. In a linked worktree the hook also staged a
second copy of each Biome-fixed file, because git gives a hook GIT_DIR
without GIT_WORK_TREE and the hook changes directory before git add.

- The hook unsets GIT_DIR and GIT_WORK_TREE, finds the project from its own
  location, and lists staged and unstaged paths relative to the project.
- staged-typecheck and dev-verify scope git output to the project and strip
  the prefix; prepare-dev-environment finds the main checkout's project
  directory, not the repository root; check-release-notes reads staged
  files with ./-relative object names.
- scripts/pre-commit-subdirectory-e2e.sh (bun run
  test:pre-commit-subdirectory) commits through the real hook in four
  layouts (root or subdirectory, normal checkout or linked worktree) and
  fails on the current main hook.

A checkout with OpenBot at the repository root behaves as before.
